// EXAMPLE ONLY -- not wired into any build. Demonstrates the same isx031-1 camera
// instance as isx031-1.json (1462 lines, hand authored MediaCtlConfig/
// supportedStreamConfig/StaticMetadata.fpsRange/vcCount/vcId/vcGroupId) reduced with the
// new self discovery path added by SensorNodeDiscovery: "discoverSensorEntity" replaces
// MediaCtlConfig entirely, and supportedStreamConfig, StaticMetadata.fpsRange and the
// virtual channel placement are all derived at runtime (via
// VIDIOC_SUBDEV_ENUM_FRAME_SIZE / VIDIOC_SUBDEV_ENUM_FRAME_INTERVAL /
// VIDIOC_SUBDEV_G_ROUTING) instead of being hand authored -- so long as the
// isx031-a-0 -> max9x -> Intel IPU7 CSI2 0 -> ISYS capture chain has already been
// linked/routed out-of-band (udev/board-init service, or kernel default routing) before
// ipu7-camera-hal starts. Note this one stub therefore covers what used to need eight
// near-identical per-virtual-channel files (isx031-1.json .. isx031-8.json), differing
// only in which sensor entity they start from: "vcId" no longer has to be hand assigned,
// it simply falls out of the stream id this sensor's data occupies on the CSI-2
// receiver, and "vcCount" falls out of how many streams that receiver multiplexes.
// Every discovered value is a fallback only: adding an explicit "vcCount"/"vcId"/
// "vcGroupId", or a "StaticMetadata" block with "fpsRange", always overrides discovery
// -- worth doing for "vcGroupId" specifically if a board needs cameras behind different
// deserializers to be mutually exclusive, since discovery conservatively reports group 0
// for all of them (see SensorNodeDiscovery::discoverVcInfo). Only "simple yuv"
// passthrough sensors/bridges (see CameraUtils::getPixelFormatFromMBusCode) qualify;
// enableAIQ/usePSysProcessor stay false exactly as in the hand authored file, since no
// ISP/PSys/3A path is involved.
//
{
  "CameraSettings": {
    "Sensor": [
      {
        "name": "isx031-1",
        "description": "isx031 as sensor (self discovered).",
        "discoverSensorEntity": "isx031 a-0",

        "enableAIQ": false,
        "usePSysProcessor": false
      }
    ]
  }
}
